The separate OpenAI packages under openai/ add focused authored skills and
reuse pinned workflow fragments. Their attribution is in openai/NOTICE.

Attribution notice per the license: when you share or adapt this plugin (or
any of the fourteen skills individually), credit Ansvar Systems AB, link to the
CC BY 4.0 license, and note any changes you made. This plugin makes no
changes to the skill text — see .github/workflows/anti-drift.yml, which
fails CI the moment a vendored copy diverges from its source.

The licence covers the skill text only. Skills 1-4 say so in a note in
their own SKILL.md; skills 5-14 state the licence in their frontmatter.
Regulatory, standards and guidance content any skill fetches at runtime
through the Ansvar Gateway MCP connector is served from its original
official publisher under that publisher's own terms, cited per row (for
example EUR-Lex content under Commission Decision 2011/833/EU; ENISA
publications under CC BY 4.0).
